          "topic": "الضَّمِير المُتَّصِل — The Pronominal Suffix",
          "note": "Table of pronominal suffixes on nouns, one column for a word without ة (بيت) and one for a word with ة (سيَّارة), per pronoun. Notes: (1) بِيتُه، سَيَّارْتُه are to be pronounced \"bēto\" \"syyārto\"; as noted in the previous lesson, the suffix for the third person masculine singular (i.e. هو) is ـه but it's not to be pronounced as an h in QA. (2) The suffixes for You plural and They (i.e. إنْتُو and هِنّ/هُمّ) vary according to dialect: in the northern dialect بِيتكُو and بيتهِن are common, and in the Jerusalem dialect بِيتكُم and بِيتهُم are common. (3) Pronominal suffixes appear also in prepositions and question words.",
          "examples": [
            {"ar": "وين + هو = وينُه؟", "en": "Where is he?"},
            {"ar": "مَعَ + إنت = مَعَك", "en": "With you"}
